      "paragraph": 1,
      "sourceLine": 3,
      "scene": 1,
      "direction": "Map head sluices, tail stair and north ladder. Perrin worked the ladder out himself. Distinguish planted support through granite from exposed gaps carried by arms and ribs. Kiva names the price without commandeering his decision; set is her contribution, not ownership of the ladder."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 52,
      "sourceLine": 107,
      "scene": 2,
      "direction": "Keep the room’s ordinary life around the serious choice. Orla describes successive rights to refuse, not a promise of consent. Aske’s rib warning has care and limited authority; humor is dry."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 67,
      "sourceLine": 139,
      "scene": 3,
      "direction": "Reset to base narrator for Mara’s viewpoint. Distinguish sea-gate tide walking fifty minutes a day from dawn spring slack held near an hour; neap slack follows the table plus twenty-three minutes. Log measurements are records, inch marks are not dialogue. Hart offers evidence without claiming a cause. Mara has still not touched a cell."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 110,
      "sourceLine": 227,
      "scene": 4,
      "direction": "Reset to Kiva. Warm on two mornings is not permission for a crossing today. Thursday remains conditional. Perrin’s Carry is his decision."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 116,
      "sourceLine": 241,
      "scene": 5,
      "direction": "Map the dummy, cloth, spar and water timetable before the run. Half sluices at bell, full at one minute, face at one twenty. Later fours can learn from earlier runs; do not accelerate the observed comparisons. End at the bell without anticipating the climb."
    }
